# docker-compose environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` (same dir) and fill in real values; `.env` is git-ignored, this
# template is not. Docker Compose auto-loads `.env` when you run compose from
# THIS directory (src/) -- which is what am7-docker-up.bat and the runbook do.
# Values here feed ${VAR} interpolation in docker-compose.yml / docker-compose.test.yml.

# ---- Embedding server -------------------------------------------------------
# The embedding endpoint URL. WORKS TODAY: this var is forwarded by the compose
# `environment:` block and substituted into web.xml (embedding.server) by
# docker/entrypoint.sh. For Azure OpenAI use the COMPLETE URL, including the
# deployment path and ?api-version=... (EmbeddingUtil POSTs to it verbatim).
#
# Local custom service example:
#   EMBEDDING_SERVER=http://192.168.1.42:8123
# Azure OpenAI example (replace resource/deployment/version):
#   EMBEDDING_SERVER=https://<resource>/openai/deployments/<deployment>/embeddings?api-version=2023-05-15
EMBEDDING_SERVER=http://192.168.1.42:8123

# ---- Embedding provider type / model / token ---------------------------------
# All three are forwarded by the compose `environment:` block and substituted
# into web.xml (embedding.type / embedding.model / embedding.authorizationToken)
# by docker/entrypoint.sh. EMBEDDING_TYPE must match EMBEDDING_SERVER's shape:
#   local         -> a custom /generate_embedding service (default, .42:8123)
#   openai        -> Azure/OpenAI: api-key header, `dimensions` sent, data[0].embedding parsed
#   openai_compat -> an OpenAI-style /v1/embeddings endpoint (Ollama, LiteLLM):
#                    `model` is REQUIRED, `dimensions` is NOT sent
#
# Ollama-container example (what am7-docker-up --ollama exports for you unless
# AM7_OLLAMA_EMBED=0 or you set these yourself):
#   EMBEDDING_SERVER=http://ollama:11434/v1/embeddings
#   EMBEDDING_TYPE=openai_compat
#   EMBEDDING_MODEL=nomic-embed-text
# Azure example:
#   EMBEDDING_TYPE=openai
#   EMBEDDING_AUTH_TOKEN=<azure-api-key>     # NEVER commit a real key
#
# EMBEDDING_TYPE=local
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=
# EMBEDDING_AUTH_TOKEN=
#
# STICKY: embedding.server is DB-overridable -- if a system.connection named
# `embedding` exists in /System's /Library/Connections (saved via the server-
# config UI or Console7), ServerConfigUtil applies ITS serverUrl/apiKey over the
# web.xml value at runtime, while embedding.type / embedding.model are read from
# web.xml (i.e. from these env vars) on EVERY boot. Changing the provider on a
# volume that holds such a record therefore needs that record updated too, or
# the URL and the type/model disagree. The wrapper keeps
# `docker-data/.embedding-provider` (format: `server type model`) and WARNS when
# the effective triple differs from the previous boot.
#
# embedding.dimensions must stay 768 to match the common.vectorExt.embedding
# column width; nomic-embed-text is natively 768 and Azure text-embedding-3-small
# honors the dimensions param AM7 sends. It is set in web.xml.template (default
# 768), not via this file. Stored vectors carry no model provenance, so switching
# embedding models silently mixes incomparable vectors in one column.

# ---- Local Ollama container (am7-docker-up --ollama, compose profile `ollama`) -
# --ollama also implies --llmproxy: LiteLLM fronts the container via the *-ctr
# aliases in litellm/config.yaml (qwen3:8b-ctr, qwen3:8b-jos-ctr,
# nomic-embed-text-ctr). ollama-init pulls OLLAMA_PULL_MODELS on first boot into
# the `ollama-models` named volume (multi-GB; watch `logs -f ollama-init`).
# Host publish is loopback-only by default; keep it that way on shared machines.
#
# OLLAMA_HOST_PORT=11435          # host port -> container :11434 (11434 is left for a host Ollama)
# OLLAMA_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1      # publish address; 0.0.0.0 exposes it to the LAN
# OLLAMA_PULL_MODELS=nomic-embed-text qwen3:8b goekdenizguelmez/JOSIEFIED-Qwen3:8b
# OLLAMA_CONTAINER_API_BASE=http://ollama:11434   # what LiteLLM's *-ctr aliases call
# OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=5m            # unload idle models (two 8B models + Langfuse + Tomcat 8g is tight)
# OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=1
#
# Wrapper-only knobs (read by am7-docker-up.sh/.bat, not by compose):
# AM7_OLLAMA_EMBED=1              # 0 = do NOT point the app's embeddings at the container
# AM7_OLLAMA_GPU=                 # `nvidia` layers in docker-compose.ollama-gpu.yml (needs nvidia-container-toolkit);
#                                 # default is CPU-only, which is the only option on the AMD Strix Halo dev box
# AM7_EXTRA_CA_FILE=              # PEM bundle for a TLS-intercepting corporate proxy; the wrappers layer
#                                 # docker-compose.extra-ca.yml when this is set OR ./volatile/extra-ca.pem
#                                 # exists (ollama pulls + LiteLLM/Azure). Build per dockerDevSetup.md §13.6.

# ---- Olio seed corpus staging (read by assemble-seed.sh, NOT by compose) -----
# assemble-seed.sh mirrors YOUR populated corpus staging dir into the docker-data
# bind mount (docker-data/am7/datagen) so the Dockerized Service7 has Olio
# reference data (names, surnames, occupations, traits, WordNet dict, optional
# location grids) without baking it into the image. Run it before you generate
# characters on a fresh stack -- see aiDocs/dockerDevSetup.md section 2e.
#
# This is consumed by the seed script (a manual pre-boot step), NOT by compose
# ${VAR} interpolation. The script reads SEED_STAGING from THIS .env directly
# (a shell does not auto-load .env the way compose does, so the script reads it
# itself). So just uncomment the line below and run, from src/:
#   cmd / PowerShell:  assemble-seed.bat            (base corpus)
#                      assemble-seed.bat --dry-run  (list only, write nothing)
#   Linux / macOS:     ./assemble-seed.sh           (base corpus)
#                      ./assemble-seed.sh --dry-run (list only, write nothing)
# assemble-seed.bat is a NATIVE Windows cmd script (uses robocopy) -- no bash,
# no Git Bash, no WSL. Use it on a Windows host; the .sh is only for Linux/macOS
# Docker hosts. Add --with-location to also copy the large grids.
# An inline/exported SEED_STAGING overrides this .env value:
#   set "SEED_STAGING=c:\other\dir" & assemble-seed.bat    (cmd)
#   SEED_STAGING=/data/other ./assemble-seed.sh            (Linux/macOS)
#
# You build the staging dir yourself (unzip seedData.7z there, add extra corpus);
# the script uses only SEED_STAGING as the source and never touches src/seedData or the .7z.
# Top-level am7/ (a live DB dir) and vault/ (secrets) are pruned and never copied,
# so SEED_STAGING may safely point at a dir that also holds those.
#
# SEED_STAGING=c:/projects/data

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres tuning for the am7-pg container (docker-compose.test.yml).
#
# Compose auto-loads THIS FILE, so anything set here silently overrides the
# build-ARG defaults in docker-compose.test.yml and docker/postgres/Dockerfile
# with nothing in either file to show it. That invisibility is the point of
# listing them here: if a pg setting is not what the compose file says it
# should be, check src/.env before anything else.
#
# All are build ARGs (they take effect on `docker compose build`) EXCEPT
# PG_SHM_SIZE, which maps to `shm_size:` and applies on container recreate with
# no build. Rationale for each value: docker/postgres/am7-tuning.conf.template.
# To retune a RUNNING stack with no rebuild, use docker/postgres/conf.d/
# instead -- see the README there.
#
# PG_IMAGE=pgvector/pgvector:0.8.6-pg18-trixie
# PG_SHARED_BUFFERS=2GB
# PG_WORK_MEM=128MB
# PG_MAINTENANCE_WORK_MEM=512MB
# PG_AUTOVACUUM_WORK_MEM=256MB
# PG_EFFECTIVE_CACHE_SIZE=8GB
# PG_RANDOM_PAGE_COST=1.1
# PG_MAX_PARALLEL_WORKERS_PER_GATHER=4
# PG_MAX_PARALLEL_MAINTENANCE_WORKERS=2
# PG_MAX_PARALLEL_WORKERS=8
# PG_EFFECTIVE_IO_CONCURRENCY=200
# PG_MAINTENANCE_IO_CONCURRENCY=200
# PG_MAX_CONNECTIONS=200
# PG_MAX_WAL_SIZE=4GB
# PG_MIN_WAL_SIZE=1GB
# PG_SHARED_PRELOAD_LIBRARIES=pg_stat_statements
# PG_SHM_SIZE=2gb
